Back in the days when I started, I had three pages of data. One was just
numbered lines, but otherwise empty, to track the dungeon levels and the
branches; I noted all fountains, altars, shops, etc. On another page all
objects detected thus far were collected. An another one I wrote all the
instrinsics gained. Don't remember what else I noted.

Currently I use the in-game possibilities to name/call objects. I've seen
people using this feature to memorize dungeon branches and the location
of chests/stashes; they name their luckstone with cryptic runes. I don't
use anything else. If I want to meorize some specific interesting scene
(like the moment where two Wizards of Yendor and the High Priest of Moloch
were killed alltogether with just one shot of a wand and by Moloch's wrath)
I just use the vim editor and a text file.

I know there have been sheets available some years ago, but unfortunately
